  "thread": "maya: quick findings from a midday a11y sweep on the new Routes dashboard \u2014 grouping a few small but actionable items so we can batch fixes :clipboard:\nmaya: 1) keyboard focus skips the route-cards when using Tab; they are clickable divs with no tabindex. users can't reach the card-level actions without a mouse\nmaya: 2) the breadcrumb has decorative separators with no role but VoiceOver reads them as \"slash\" which is noisy\nmaya: 3) route status chips rely only on color; no aria-label or text for assistive tech\nmaya: 4) compact-mode tooltips are not keyboard-accessible and use CSS-only hover for visibility\n\nanya: good catches. for cards we should make the outer wrapper a `<button>` or add `tabindex=0 role=button` and keyboard handlers. prefer semantic button for ease of a11y and reduced JS\n\nsam: breadcrumb separators: add `aria-hidden=true` on separators or render them via CSS `::before` so SRs skip them. that removes the noisy \"slash\" reads\n\nfrank: status chips: add sr-only text like `<span class=\"sr-only\">Status: healthy</span>` or use `role=img aria-label` if we want the visual dot + label. avoid duplicating visible text for SRs\n\nmaya: tooltips: change hover-only to a focusable trigger (`button` or `tabindex=0`) and ensure `aria-describedby` points to the tooltip with `role=tooltip`. add keyboard handlers for Enter/Space and Esc to close\n\na11y-bot: nightly scan (routes-dashboard/2026-04-01) 7 issues flagged: 4 medium (focusable content not reachable; decorative content read by SR; tooltip not accessible). Report: https://ci.redwood/axe/scan/3721 :warning:\n\nanya: prioritization: 1) make route-cards keyboard-focusable (critical for keyboard users) 2) tooltip keyboard access 3) status chip aria labels 4) breadcrumb separators. I'll create tickets and assign estimates\n\nmaya: i can take cards + chips. sam takes tooltip changes. frank can handle breadcrumb and theme tokens if contrast issues pop up while we're here\n\nsam: for tooltips i'll add an e2e keyboard test and a unit test to assert `aria-describedby` exists and the tooltip becomes visible on Enter and focus moves appropriately. adding storybook knobs for keyboard demo too\n\nfrank: i'll also run the after-change axe scan and post results here. recommend adding acceptance criteria: tab into cards, press Enter to open; SR reads status for focused card; tooltip reachable with keyboard and announced. include short repro steps in PR\n\nmaya: created issues #5710 #5711 #5712 and added links to the bot scan. opening PRs as drafts and will tag `@design` + `@eng-accessibility` for quick review. closing thread when PRs have green scans\n\nanya: thanks team. small incremental changes but will improve keyboard-only flows a lot. :sparkles:",
